// Domain 3 — Integration flashcards (FortiNAC-F 7.6).
export default [
  // 3.1
  { id: 'd3-f001', topic: '3.1', front: 'Three prerequisites before FortiNAC-F processes pushed syslog or traps?', back: '`syslog`/`snmp` in port1 `allowaccess`; the sender **modeled** with the IP it sources messages from; a definition (Syslog File, security event parser or Trap MIB File).' },
  { id: 'd3-f002', topic: '3.1', front: 'How is a firewall or IPS that only sends syslog modeled?', back: 'As a **pingable device** (Network > Inventory > Add Pingable Device) with **Incoming Events** = Syslog or Security Events.' },
  { id: 'd3-f003', topic: '3.1', front: 'Incoming Events: Syslog vs Security Events?', back: '**Syslog** applies a Syslog File and creates standard events. **Security Events** applies a security event parser for Security Incidents (licensed).' },
  { id: 'd3-f004', topic: '3.1', front: 'Three formats supported by Syslog Files and security event parsers?', back: '**CSV** (by column number), **TAG/VALUE** (by tag, space delimiter, quoted values with spaces) and **CEF** (fixed pipe header + tagged extensions).' },
  { id: 'd3-f005', topic: '3.4', front: 'What does the Vendor OUI table do?', back: 'Validates MACs (unknown OUI = invalid address), shows the **Vendor Alias** as host name, gives a role for portal-registered devices and a registration type. Updated by AutoDef Synchronization; F 7.6.7 adds regex OUIs.' },
  { id: 'd3-f006', topic: '3.1', front: 'Why use MAC notification traps instead of linkUp/linkDown?', back: 'The trap carries the MAC and port, so FortiNAC-F needn\'t read the forwarding table. Also works behind IP phones and hubs. Enable on access ports only and remove link traps there.' },
  { id: 'd3-f007', topic: '3.1', front: 'SNMP versions for switch MAC notification traps vs custom Trap MIB File traps?', back: 'MAC notification: **v1, v2 and v3**. Trap MIB Files: documented as **v1 and v2 only**.' },
  { id: 'd3-f008', topic: '3.1', front: 'Trap MIB File custom trap: key fields?', back: 'Enterprise OID, Specific Type, IP/MAC/User ID OID (any one), Alarm Cause, Event Format with `{n}` varbinds counted from 0.' },
  { id: 'd3-f009', topic: '3.4', front: 'Device profiling rules and MDM hosts?', back: 'Profiling evaluates **rogues only**, so MDM-registered hosts are skipped. Within a rule **all** selected methods must match. Use **Run** to re-evaluate online rogues.' },
  { id: 'd3-f010', topic: '3.1', front: 'Default admin group for alarm-triggered email?', back: '**All Management**. Holds admin and root at first; new admins are added automatically. Create your own admin groups to target notifications.' },
  { id: 'd3-f011', topic: '3.1', front: 'Prerequisites for alarm email and SMS to admins?', back: 'Email: an email address on each admin plus Email Settings (SMTP server). SMS: Mobile Number and Mobile Provider on each admin.' },
  { id: 'd3-f012', topic: '3.1', front: 'Four alarm trigger rules?', back: 'One Event to One Alarm; All Events to One Alarm; **Event Frequency** (N per element in a sliding window); **Event Lifetime** (no clearing event within the time).' },
  { id: 'd3-f013', topic: '3.1', front: 'Log receiver types and default ports?', back: 'Syslog CSV and Syslog CEF: 514 (Facility default 4). SNMP Trap: 162 (Security String). FortiAnalyzer: TCP 514 with the FAZ serial number.' },
  { id: 'd3-f014', topic: '3.1', front: 'Receiver configured but no events reach the SIEM. First check?', back: 'The event\'s logging option must be **External** or **Internal & External**. For alarms, the mapping needs **Send Alarm to External Log Hosts**.' },
  { id: 'd3-f015', topic: '3.4', front: 'MDM attributes usable in user/host profiles?', back: '**Managed by MDM** (all), Compliant, Passcode Enabled, Data Encryption, Compromised (vendor-dependent). If the MDM user isn\'t in FortiNAC-F, the host is registered as a device with NAC-Default.' },
  // 3.2
  { id: 'd3-f016', topic: '3.2', front: 'Steps to let FortiNAC-M manage a CA?', back: 'Same build; `nac-ipc` + `ssh` on port1 of both; `globaloptiontool -name security.allowedserialnumbers -setRaw "…"` (Manager lists all, CA lists Manager); restart services; add the CA in **CA Management**.' },
  { id: 'd3-f017', topic: '3.2', front: 'Global objects synchronized from the Manager?', back: 'Admin profiles, guest templates, device profiling rules, device types, groups, roles, user/host profiles, endpoint compliance policies/configs/scans (+ their security actions). Read-only on CAs.' },
  { id: 'd3-f018', topic: '3.2', front: 'Global Object Synchronization interval, and what Synchronize Now does?', back: 'Automatic on a fixed timer (the 7.6.3+ guide says 10 min; another page says once a minute, so do not memorise the number); older CA data is overwritten. Synchronize Now overwrites all globally shared data on the CA immediately.' },
  { id: 'd3-f019', topic: '3.2', front: 'Host/user propagation from F 7.6.3?', back: 'The Manager syncs host (by MAC) and user (by user ID) records among CAs every **5 min**, under **On Demand Host Propagation**. User-registered hosts also need **Propagate Hosts** on the user.' },
  { id: 'd3-f020', topic: '3.2', front: 'Are guest accounts synchronized between CAs?', back: 'No. They\'re **copied on demand** by the Manager when a guest registers elsewhere. If the Manager is down, guests can\'t register on a CA without their account.' },
  { id: 'd3-f021', topic: '3.2', front: 'Licensing with FortiNAC-M?', back: 'One concurrent pool held by the Manager, shared by all CAs. A feature in the Manager key applies to all CAs; for one CA only, put it in that CA key and not the Manager\'s. CAs keep running if the Manager is down.' },
  { id: 'd3-f022', topic: '3.2', front: 'What did 7.6.0 change for FortiNAC-M HA pairs?', back: 'Replaced by **Cluster Management** (one leader, workers with Config Wizard-only UI). Both Managers become active; the VIP is removed.' },
  // 3.3
  { id: 'd3-f023', topic: '3.3', front: 'How does FortiNAC-F lift a VPN user\'s restriction?', back: 'Sends the logical network\'s **firewall tag/group via FSSO** to the FortiGate, so a policy using that FSSO group matches. It never terminates the VPN or assigns a VLAN.' },
  { id: 'd3-f024', topic: '3.3', front: 'FortiGate syslog requirements for VPN integration?', back: 'Syslog to FortiNAC-F port1 (not the VPN interface); `source-ip` = modeled FortiGate IP; log IDs 0101039947/48 (SSL), 0101037129/34 and **0101037139** (IPsec, F 7.6+).' },
  { id: 'd3-f025', topic: '3.3', front: 'Tunnel DNS settings for a FortiNAC-managed VPN?', back: 'DNS 1 = production, **DNS 2 = FortiNAC-F VPN interface**, domain/DNS suffix = **FortiNAC-F VPN scope domain** (agents use SRV lookups; avoid `.local`).' },
  { id: 'd3-f026', topic: '3.3', front: 'VPN interface on the FortiGate model shows Uplink. Fix?', back: 'It must be Device or Multiple Hosts. Raise **System Defined Uplink Count** above peak concurrent VPN users (Network > Settings > Network Device).' },
  { id: 'd3-f027', topic: '3.3', front: 'FSSO connector vs Security Fabric ports?', back: 'FSSO: TCP **8000** (`fsso` allowaccess; `config user fsso` on FortiGate). Fabric: FortiNAC-F → root FortiGate on **8013**, then authorize on the root.' },
  // 3.4
  { id: 'd3-f028', topic: '3.4', front: 'MDM: On Demand Registration vs Automatic Registration Polling?', back: 'On Demand: query the MDM when an unknown host **reaches the captive portal**. Polling: periodically import the whole MDM inventory and register every device as **Managed by MDM**.' },
];
